From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:08:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 381/443] [ae-patch] Fix the voice log, meter and approval
 review findings (0381)

Meter off: a take with no recognizer activity for 10 s after audiostart gets a fresh recognizer silently (log "mic idle recycle", never reported deaf), at most 6 a minute, then "mic idle recycle capped" until the next result. The event stall detector counts speech only on speechstart or a soundstart that lasted 600 ms before its soundend, also fires 6 s after the last sound or speech event when no end event came, and restarts silently without ever escalating to "stalled repeatedly". The Level meter setting is a dependency of the meter effect, so a change mid-take opens or closes the second stream.
Approvals: the voice answer is marked only after the POST went through (a card that is pending again is a failure: the id is forgotten and "approval answer failed" is logged), and approvalOf matches the registered ae_slot_cap policy name exactly.
Voice log: a throttled Voice-end upload shows no toast; page-hide uploads use the new reason page_hidden with a 60 s budget of their own; a keepalive request is retried without keepalive only after a non-abort failure while the page is visible.
Server: the resolve route logs after a successful resolve, with ids as %r capped at 120 characters.
